# Only Go sources, templates/ and static/ are needed to build the image (see Dockerfile).
# Anything else dropped into the project directory (OTA images, APKs, dumps, backups)
# would otherwise be streamed to the daemon as build context on every build.
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
.env
.env.*
docs
*.md
tools
docker-compose*.yml
# Runtime settings written by a running server (root-owned in some setups, and it can
# hold API keys). Never copied into the image, so it has no business in the context.
config
Dockerfile*
data
uploads
backups
tmp
*.img
*.zip
*.apk
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.sql
*.dump
*.log

# The client submodules (Kotlin/Java, AOSP). They are in this repo so the whole
# MDM is one clone, but nothing in them is built into the server image, and
# unignored they stream ~150MB to the daemon as build context on every build.
aio-mdm-client
aio-mdm-client-dpc
aio-mdm-lite
aio-mdm-client-lite
